From: Athena Build <athena@local>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: rules: tolerate missing doc files in override_dh_installdocs (nodoc)
Origin: vendor
Bug-Athena: p7zip override_dh_installdocs fails under DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-19

debian/rules' override_dh_installdocs target runs:

    cd debian/p7zip-full/usr/share/doc/p7zip && \
        mv `cat ../../../../../p7zip-full.docs | cut -b5-` DOC/

This relies on `dh_installdocs --link-doc=p7zip` having just staged
the files listed in debian/p7zip-full.docs (DOC/7zC.txt, DOC/lzma.txt
etc.) into debian/p7zip-full/usr/share/doc/p7zip/.  Under
DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc, dh_installdocs is a no-op — no files staged
— and the unconditional mv fails:

    mv: cannot stat '7zC.txt': No such file or directory
    mv: cannot stat '7zFormat.txt': No such file or directory
    ...
    make[1]: *** [debian/rules:72: override_dh_installdocs] Error 1

Fix: loop the .docs entries and only move files that actually exist
in the staged doc tree.  Behaviour with the manual present (default
upstream build) is unchanged — every listed file exists, all moved.

TEMPORARY: nodoc is a workaround for missing doc-build tooling in
the build pool, not a permanent policy.  DELETE THIS PATCH when
CONF-08 lands and nodoc is dropped from [Source] BuildOptions /
BuildProfiles in config/build.conf.

This supersedes the 16.02+dfsg-8 era patch (9001-graceful-skip-
when-manual-absent.patch) which targeted a different failure mode
(debian/p7zip-full.links absent in this newer source).
---
 debian/rules | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -70,4 +70,7 @@
 	dh_installdocs --link-doc=p7zip
 #	p7zip compat - move documents to DOC/
 	mkdir -p -m 755 debian/p7zip-full/usr/share/doc/p7zip/DOC/
-	cd debian/p7zip-full/usr/share/doc/p7zip && mv `cat ../../../../../p7zip-full.docs | cut -b5-` DOC/
+	cd debian/p7zip-full/usr/share/doc/p7zip && \
+	  for f in $$(cat ../../../../../p7zip-full.docs | cut -b5-); do \
+	    if [ -e "$$f" ]; then mv "$$f" DOC/; fi; \
+	  done
